nnects to the tables I'm planning. The first experiment covers R² profiles for both trained and untrained models, L1 attention routing comparisons, cross-instruction classification performance, CF sensitivity analysis, and RSA results. The second experiment shows similar analyses but with the spatial variant, including that inverted CF sensitivity finding. Let me structure the paper to systematically present all these results. I'm setting up the LaTeX document with a two-column format and standard packages, then structuring the paper into five main sections: an introduction covering VLAs and our interpretability framework, a brief related work section, a methods section detailing the five analysis techniques, experimental setup covering the architectures and datasets, and results with the tables from my experiments. Writing the LaTeX document...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15507,"cache_read_input_tokens":23396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15507},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a40ae5d-f3e6-4fa0-9a07-a3bfe69d2f75","uuid":"0e54b487-76d4-4cae-abd7-46a5f45e85eb"}
